> ## Comment/code mismatches and important issues
> 
> 1. **“Fixed 2020 shares” is not guaranteed.**  
>    The code uses configurable `pop_weight_year`:
>    ```r
>    wy <- config$aggregation$pop_weight_year
>    ghs_base <- ghs[year == wy, ...]
>    ```
>    Thus the comment is only correct when `wy == 2020`. Either enforce that or say “fixed `pop_weight_year` shares.” The historical logic likewise depends on `wy`:
>    ```r
>    ghs_ys <- ghs[year >= 1990 & year < wy, ...]
>    ```
> 
> 2. **Partial national-control coverage produces missing years, not frozen values.**  
>    A country is considered covered if it appears in *any* `proj_nat` row:
>    ```r
>    nat_countries <- unique(proj_nat$iso3)
>    ```
>    If it lacks, say, 2075–2100 controls, it is omitted for those years rather than frozen. The same applies historically. The stated “countries without a control total” fallback should operate by `iso3 × year`, not country alone.
> 
> 3. **The code does not enforce the documented 2020–2100 projection span.**  
>    `proj` inherits whatever year range exists in `proj_nat`; `frozen` uses that same observed range:
>    ```r
>    proj_years <- range(proj_nat$year)
>    ```
>    Explicitly construct `2020:2100` and validate national control coverage.
> 
> 4. **Zero GHS national population breaks national accounting in projection.**  
>    Projection directly divides by `ghs_nat`:
>    ```r
>    proj[, pop := ghs_ir * (nat * 1e6) / ghs_nat]
>    ```
>    A zero or missing `ghs_nat` yields `Inf`/`NA`. Historical data instead assigns zero shares, causing IR population to sum to zero rather than the national control total. Both cases need an explicit fallback or failure.
> 
> 5. **WPP variant selection is not visible here.**  
>    The comment promises estimates through 2023 and the medium variant afterwards, but this code just uses:
>    ```r
>    wpp <- read_wpp(config)
>    ```
>    That is correct only if `read_wpp()` already filters to precisely that series. Make the selection explicit or document the invariant.
> 
> 6. **`pop_linear_annual()` does not fully “pass annual input through unchanged.”**  
>    It drops countries with only one positive observation and does not check duplicate `iso3, year` keys. Validate uniqueness and decide whether one-knot series should be retained, frozen, or rejected.
> 
> 7. **Add accounting tests.**  
>    For each controlled country-year with valid GHS shares, assert:
>    ```r
